We are looking for a Business Process Engineer for our customer in Kortenberg
<br>
<br>Main tasks and responsibilities:
<br>
<br>This role fits in the implementation and introduction of a new ERP and other systms for providing services to our customers. Togetherwith the European team, you will be analyzing the existing processes and defining the best practices and contribute to a succesfull roll-out and maintenance of the new ERP system and other systems.
<br>
<br>Investigating and Analyzing current business processes, procedures and requirements and mapping them to SharePoint;
<br>Documenting visualization of process and procedure flows;
<br>Identification and assessment of potential risks in business processes and development of risk mitigation strategies;
<br>Re-engineering and optimization of business processes and shaping new process policies;
<br>Proposing smarter process management solutions for performance improvement and cost reduction;
<br>Illustrating project descriptions, objectives, and measurements;
<br>Collaboration with various stakeholders to identify potential for improvement;
<br>Participate in and hold meetings to perform incremental agile software development framework when managing product development;
<br>Support to evaluate and test administrative system changes to provide ongoing support to existing applications and implement new applications;
<br>Staying updated with new software features and industry trends and educating people in the group.
Profile:
<br>Several years of experience in business process analysis and optimization;
<br>Strong analytical and problem-solving skills;
<br>Ability to critically question processes;
<br>Excellent communication and teamwork skills;
<br>Accuracy and care in the analysis and documentation of processes;
<br>Language skills in English mandatory.
<br>
<br>Professional skills:
<br>Excellent knowledge of Business Process Modeling, Business Process Reengineering and the related Management (BPM) Tools;
<br>SharePoint: Knowledge in using SharePoint for mapping business requirements and managing document workflows;
<br>Data Analysis Tools: Skills in using tools like Excel or Power BI for analyzing business data and visualizing process flows;
<br>
<br>Nice to have:
<br>
<br>Knowledge in SAP S/4HANA public cloud;
<br>Agile Frameworks: Understanding and applying agile methodologies for software development and project management;
<br>Software Testing: Experience in professional software testing and quality assurance;
<br>Experience in Project Management and related Software is an advantage: Experience with tools like JIRA, Trello, or Microsoft Project for managing tasks and tracking progress;
<br>Programming Languages: A basic understanding of programming languages like Python, Java, or C# can be advantageous for accurately assessing the feasibility of proposed changes.

